12
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
George of the Jungle is a 1997 American comedy film directed by Sam Weisman.

13
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
It is based on the 1967 American animated television series of the same name created by Jay Ward and
Bill Scott, which parodied the fictional character Tarzan by Edgar Rice Burroughs.

14
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
The screenplay was written by Dana Olsen and Audrey Wells.

15
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
The film stars Brendan Fraser as the title character, alongside Leslie Mann, Thomas
Haden Church, Holland Taylor, Richard Roundtree, and John Cleese.

16
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
The plot follows a man who was raised by animals in the jungle and later falls in love
with a wealthy heiress, leading to conflict with her self-absorbed fiancé.

17
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:06,000
Produced by Walt Disney Pictures, the film was released theatrically
in the United States and Canada on July 16, 1997.

18
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
It premiered on the Disney Channel in the United States on December 5, 1998.

19
01:16:00,000 --> 01:16:06,000
The film received mixed reviews from critics but was a
commercial success grossing $174 million worldwide.

20
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:06,000
A direct-to-video sequel, George of the Jungle 2,
was released on October 21, 2003.

21
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The film explores themes of san francisco,
california, africa, gorilla, narration, lion.

22
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:06,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and thought_provoking.
